$ w tungsten

  ◆ tungsten · W · 74
  │ atomic mass    183.84 u
  │ density        19.3 g/cm³
  │ melting point  3421.85 °C
  │ boiling point  5554.85 °C
  │ state          solid
  │ category       transition metal
  │ discovered     1783
  │ named          From Swedish tung sten, 'heavy stone'. Its symbol W is from
  │   wolfram, after the ore wolframite: German Wolf Rahm, 'wolf's froth',
  │   because the ore devoured tin during smelting.

  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── W74
